-- Rewrite option text so the correct answer no longer stands out by length.
--
-- The seed bank's correct option was the longest in 329 of 350 questions, so
-- "pick the longest answer" scored about 94% with no knowledge. The seed files
-- were rewritten (mostly longer distractors, some tighter correct answers) and
-- seeds/generate_coverage.py now fails on the pattern. Bulk import rejects
-- titles that already exist, so a database seeded before the rewrite only gets
-- the new text through this migration.
--
-- Each row is matched on (category slug, question title, old text). An option
-- already edited through the admin console no longer matches and is left
-- alone, and rerunning the migration is a no-op. Only text changes: ids,
-- positions and is_correct are untouched, so past attempts stay valid.

BEGIN;

UPDATE question_options
SET option_text = changes.new_text
FROM (VALUES
